00:36:32,900 --> 00:36:34,067
好了，该干正事了。
Right, we've got work to do.

706
00:36:35,733 --> 00:36:37,433
我是这么想的，把松鼠架在烤网上面，
I'm thinking
squirrel on the rack,

707
00:36:37,467 --> 00:36:39,700
然后呢，我的计划是这样，
and then maybe,
here's my plan,

708
00:36:39,733 --> 00:36:44,000
撒点香草，稍微点缀一下，差不多就这样。
with a few herbs, garnished,
something like that.

709
00:36:44,033 --> 00:36:47,167
呃，我在琢磨要是先烤上一遍，
Um, I'm thinking
if I cook it once,

710
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:49,200
然后回炉再烤一遍，
and then maybe cook it again,

711
00:36:49,233 --> 00:36:50,900
口感就会变得跟香酥鸭一样，
so it'll go like crispy duck,

712
00:36:50,933 --> 00:36:52,133
只不过原料换成了松鼠。
only it's a squirrel.

713
00:36:56,500 --> 00:36:58,167
他到底还回不回来了？
Is he ever coming back?

714
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:00,100
我们总不能直接扔上去烤吧？
We can't just
lob it on, can we?

715
00:37:00,133 --> 00:37:03,100
要是兔子的话倒还好办，
把头剁掉，然后从正中间开膛……
Okay with the rabbit,
you take the head off and
you go down the middle...

716
00:37:03,133 --> 00:37:05,700
可我们手头能拿来下刀的
就只有一根营钉。
But all we've got
to do it with
is a tent pick.

717
00:37:05,733 --> 00:37:08,200
- 你没带折叠小刀吗？
- 没带。
-Didn't you bring a penknife?
-No.

718
00:37:11,167 --> 00:37:15,867
哈蒙德：时间一分一秒过去，
杰里米依然不见踪影。
HAMMOND: Time passed,
and still no sign of Jeremy.

719
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:17,233
哥们，我可不剥皮。
I'm not peeling it, mate.

720
00:37:17,267 --> 00:37:18,633
凭什么非得我来干这个。
I don't see
why I should do it.

721
00:37:18,667 --> 00:37:20,433
-快点吧。
-我才不要给松鼠剥皮。
-Come on.
-I don't want to
peel a squirrel.

722
00:37:20,467 --> 00:37:21,733
我这就把松鼠给你拿过去。
I'm gonna bring the squirrel
over to you.

723
00:37:21,767 --> 00:37:23,200
-（鸣笛声）
-是辆车吗？
-(HORN BLARES)
-Is that a car?

724
00:37:23,233 --> 00:37:24,233
是大猩猩吗？
Is it Jezza?

725
00:37:25,700 --> 00:37:27,367
詹姆斯？
James?

726
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:30,267
-他车上拉的什么？
-说正经的，
那简直……
-What's he got?
-In all seriousness,
that's...

727
00:37:31,267 --> 00:37:32,867
什么鬼？
What?

728
00:37:32,867 --> 00:37:34,533
（大笑）
(LAUGHS)

729
00:37:34,567 --> 00:37:36,967
你特么一定是在……
You have got to be...

730
00:37:48,667 --> 00:37:50,433
伙计，那是一整头死牛啊！
It's a flaming cow, mate!

731
00:38:01,867 --> 00:38:03,900
-今晚主菜。
-是啊。
-Main course.
-Yeah.

732
00:38:03,933 --> 00:38:06,533
我在琢磨我是不是在太阳底下
搭帐篷给晒迷糊了。
I'm thinking how long
have I've been in the sun
putting the tent up.

733
00:38:06,567 --> 00:38:10,100
-怎么说？
-因为我眼前的画面……
-你肯定会喜欢的。
-Why?
-Because what I'm seeing...
You'll love this.

734
00:38:10,133 --> 00:38:12,200
……是你卡迈罗车顶上绑了头牛。
Is a cow on the roof
of your Camaro.

735
00:38:12,233 --> 00:38:14,967
可不是嘛！
上面真真切切躺着一头牛。
It is, isn't it?
That is a cow on there.

736
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:17,267
我不是想挑刺啊，
但这是路毙动物吗？
I don't want to be pedantic,
but is it road kill?

737
00:38:17,300 --> 00:38:19,033
什么意思，你怀疑是我撞死的？
What, are you suggesting
I ran it down?

738
00:38:19,067 --> 00:38:20,967
-这个嘛……
-看看我车头。
-Well...
-Check out the front
of my car.

739
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:24,433
我是找了个人帮我把它抬上去的，
但我可没撞它。
I had to find someone to
help me get it on there,
but I didn't run it down.

740
00:38:24,467 --> 00:38:28,233
它本来就倒在路边，
现在绑上了车顶，
它现在就是咱们的晚餐了！
It was at the side of the road
and now it's on the roof
and now it's our supper!

741
00:38:28,267 --> 00:38:29,700
你知道这玩意儿该怎么料理吗？
Do you know
what to do with it?

742
00:38:29,733 --> 00:38:31,667
-额，你得……
-给它剥皮。
-Well, you've got to...
-Peel it.

743
00:38:31,700 --> 00:38:33,867
-（大笑）
-我才不剥那玩意儿！
-(LAUGHS)
-I'm not peeling that!

744
00:38:35,067 --> 00:38:37,767
梅：不过首先，
我们得把它从车顶上弄下来。
MAY: First though,
we had to get it off the roof.

745
00:38:37,867 --> 00:38:41,533
要是我猛倒车急转弯会怎样？
What if I go round a corner
quite quickly, backwards?

746
00:38:41,567 --> 00:38:43,400
-要是挂倒挡的话。
-左打死，对。
-If I reverse.
-Left hand down, yeah.

747
00:38:43,433 --> 00:38:46,400
方向盘向左打死，
它就会往那边滚下去，你觉得呢？
Left hand down,
it'll roll over that way,
do we think?

748
00:38:46,433 --> 00:38:47,933
我觉得万事俱备，开整吧。
I reckon she's good to go.

749
00:38:50,933 --> 00:38:53,067
漂亮，搞定！
Yes, there you go!

750
00:38:53,733 --> 00:38:55,400
-嘿，杰里米？
-干嘛？
-Hey, Jeremy?
-What?

751
00:38:55,433 --> 00:38:58,467
我病好了，
我已经看不到你卡迈罗车顶上有牛了。
I'm better,
I can't see a cow on the roof
of your Camaro any more.

752
00:38:58,500 --> 00:39:00,367
-我还不饿。
-什么？
-I'm not hungry.
-What?

753
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:01,867
我不饿。
I'm not hungry.

754
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,433
你个混……
You son...

755
00:39:04,033 --> 00:39:05,600
臭死了，杰里米。
It stinks, Jeremy.

756
00:39:09,567 --> 00:39:13,533
克拉克森：那晚，
断背山哈蒙德和我饱餐了一顿牛肉加松鼠，
CLARKSON: That night,
Brokeback and I feasted
on beef and squirrel,

757
00:39:13,567 --> 00:39:15,033
等梅睡下之后，
and then, with May in bed,

758
00:39:15,067 --> 00:39:17,167
我们一致认定，对大伙儿来说最好的安排，
we decided it would be
better for all of us

759
00:39:17,200 --> 00:39:20,867
就是让他车里的空调“刚好”坏掉。
if the air-conditioning
in his car were to break.

760
00:39:31,867 --> 00:39:33,167
克拉克森：嘘！
哈蒙德：好。
CLARKSON: Shh!
HAMMOND: Okay.

761
00:39:33,667 --> 00:39:35,067
对不住！
Sorry!

762
00:39:36,133 --> 00:39:37,867
干嘛不直接拿锤子砸呢？
Why don't we just hit it
with a hammer?

763
00:39:37,867 --> 00:39:39,300
（哈蒙德大笑）
(HAMMOND LAUGHING)

764
00:39:40,167 --> 00:39:41,067
等会儿。
Hold on.

765
00:39:41,100 --> 00:39:42,467
哎，等等，等等！
Oh, hang on, hang on!

766
00:39:44,467 --> 00:39:47,133
（大笑）
(LAUGHING)

767
00:39:47,167 --> 00:39:49,933
这帮人真是拿大巴底盘造的这车，太离谱了！
They really built these
on buses. It's ridiculous!

768
00:39:49,967 --> 00:39:51,967
（克拉克森大笑）
(CLARKSON LAUGHING)

769
00:39:52,967 --> 00:39:54,967
我拿锅铲拍它呢。
I'm just hitting it
with a spatula.

770
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,000
又有一只蚊子叮我脸上了。
Another mosquito
just bit my face.

771
00:39:57,033 --> 00:39:58,700
根本没用啊。
It's not working.

772
00:39:58,733 --> 00:40:00,167
（克拉克森大笑）
(CLARKSON LAUGHING)

773
00:40:08,867 --> 00:40:10,867
他绝对会看出来的，对吧？
He's gonna notice, isn't he?

774
00:40:17,100 --> 00:40:19,100
哈蒙德：又一个闷热潮湿的黎明到来了，
HAMMOND: Another
humid day dawned,

775
00:40:19,133 --> 00:40:21,867
现在梅终于体会到这种滋味了。
and now May knew
what it felt like.

776
00:40:22,700 --> 00:40:25,100
梅：那几个成天灌着廉价啤酒、
MAY: Those pathetic,

777
00:40:25,133 --> 00:40:29,433
啃着烤肉、红脖子暴徒般的
lager-swilling,
barbecuing, redneck thugs

778
00:40:29,467 --> 00:40:32,900
所谓“联合主持人”，把我的车给祸害了。
that I call my co-presenters
have vandalised my car.

779
00:40:37,067 --> 00:40:41,967
克拉克森：今天早上我不得不对这辆车
进行一点小小的改装，
CLARKSON: I have had to make
a few modifications
to the car this morning

780
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,900
因为那起“死牛事故”，我的收音机天线断了。
because of the cow incident,
I lost the aerial.

781
00:40:44,933 --> 00:40:47,367
所以现在我改用了一个i-Station便携音响。
So now I've got
an i-Station instead.

782
00:40:47,400 --> 00:40:49,167
但把这玩意儿和那个风扇摆在一起，结果就是——
And that, teamed
with the fan means

783
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:51,267
我完全看不清前方的路了。
I really can't see
where I'm going.

784
00:40:51,300 --> 00:40:54,333
还有，因为确实有部分死牛组织渗进了车里，
Also, because some cow
did get into the car,

785
00:40:54,367 --> 00:40:56,233
我在这里挂了些空气清新剂来压盖臭味。
I'm using air fresheners here
to cover up the smell.

786
00:40:56,267 --> 00:40:59,100
这下好了，后视镜也全挡住了，我连走过的路也看不见了。
So I can't really see
where I've been.

787
00:40:59,133 --> 00:41:01,733
哦，还有副驾驶座，
Oh, and the passenger seat,

788
00:41:01,767 --> 00:41:03,533
上面沾满了牛身上的脓汁，
that got a lot of
cow juice on it,

789
00:41:03,567 --> 00:41:05,933
所以我把它扔到了哈蒙德的皮卡货斗里。
so it's now in the back of
Hammond's truck.

790
00:41:09,933 --> 00:41:11,100
电台男主播：预计今天下午，
MAN ON RADIO:
By this afternoon,

791
00:41:11,133 --> 00:41:12,667
天空将出现大片阴云，
skies will be
considerably cloudy

792
00:41:12,700 --> 00:41:14,900
极可能伴有阵雨及雷暴天气。
with showers and
thunder storms likely.

793
00:41:14,933 --> 00:41:18,033
东北风，风速每小时5到10英里。
North east winds,
five to 10 miles per hour.

794
00:41:18,700 --> 00:41:19,733
冲啊！
Come on!

795
00:41:19,767 --> 00:41:22,500
离阿拉巴马只剩40英里了！
Alabama's only 40 miles now!

796
00:41:24,133 --> 00:41:28,333
我们这几辆报废场淘来的破车已经跑了650英里，不可避免地，
Our scrap yard cars
have covered 650 miles
and inevitably

797
00:41:28,367 --> 00:41:31,967
它们在心中已不再只是一堆冰冷的废铁。
they were becoming
more than just metal.

798
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:36,000
这一路的一切，真真切切诠释了我为何如此热爱汽车。
This whole thing now really
sums up why I love cars.

799
00:41:36,033 --> 00:41:37,467
就拿这台科迈罗来说吧，
Now you take this Camaro,

800
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:41,533
它的仪表盘比美国的新闻主播还要假、还要塑料感十足，
the dash is more plastic than
an American newsreader,

801
00:41:41,567 --> 00:41:43,533
这引擎的动力比比利时还弱，
the engine's got
less power than Belgium,

802
00:41:43,567 --> 00:41:47,867
悬挂比机上航空杂志的文章
还要软趴趴，
the suspension is softer
than the journalism
in an in-flight magazine,

803
00:41:47,867 --> 00:41:51,000
当然了，
闻起来还一股死牛臭。
and of course,
it reeks of cow.

804
00:41:51,033 --> 00:41:52,867
但我爱死它了，
But, I adore it,

805
00:41:52,867 --> 00:41:57,167
因为你能明显感觉到
它还想继续跑下去。
because you can just sense
it wants to keep going.

806
00:41:57,200 --> 00:42:01,133
我敢打赌开着凯迪拉克的詹姆斯
肯定也深有同感。
And I bet James is
exactly the same there
in the Cadillac.

807
00:42:01,167 --> 00:42:05,233
我打赌他现在心里
绝对是一模一样的情感。
I bet he's having
exactly the same emotions.

808
00:42:05,267 --> 00:42:09,500
我宁愿现在坐在这台车里，
也不去坐法拉利恩佐，绝不开玩笑。
I'd rather be in this now
than an Enzo,
and I'm not joking.

809
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:12,567
哈蒙德：不过在进入阿拉巴马州之前，
HAMMOND: But before
we entered Alabama,

810
00:42:12,600 --> 00:42:15,433
我们必须先去“巴格达”
迎接下一个挑战。
we had to go to Bagdad
for our next challenge.

811
00:42:22,533 --> 00:42:23,600
到了，就这儿！
This is it!

812
00:42:24,367 --> 00:42:25,933
我们到巴格达了。
We are in Bagdad.

813
00:42:25,967 --> 00:42:29,967
这趟旅行我真没想到
会跑来这种地方。
Not a place I was expecting
to visit on this trip.

814
00:42:46,933 --> 00:42:48,333
挑战时间到。
Challenge time.

815
00:42:49,500 --> 00:42:51,767
“一小时内减重五磅。”
Lose five pounds in one hour.

816
00:42:51,867 --> 00:42:54,600
对，把汗全蒸出来！
来吧，搞起。
Yep, sweat it away!
Come on then.

817
00:42:54,633 --> 00:42:56,867
不是这个。
No.

818
00:42:56,867 --> 00:43:00,000
好吧，上面写着：
我们横穿骄傲的阿拉巴马州时，
Okay. It says here,
we must not be
shot or arrested

819
00:43:00,033 --> 00:43:02,933
绝对不能被人开枪击中
或是被警察逮捕。
as we drive across
the proud state of Alabama.

820
00:43:02,967 --> 00:43:08,233
但如果我们能害另外两人
挨枪子或被抓，就能拿到奖励分。
But we will get bonus points
if we can get one of
the others shot or arrested.

821
00:43:08,267 --> 00:43:11,667
我没搞懂，
这要怎么操作？
I don't understand.
How do we do that?

822
00:43:11,700 --> 00:43:13,300
“因此，你们要互相装饰对方的车，
You will therefore decorate
one another's cars

823
00:43:13,333 --> 00:43:16,100
尽可能在这个笃信圣经、
in such a way to draw
maximum attention to yourself

824
00:43:16,133 --> 00:43:18,333
红脖子遍地、
in this Bible-bashing,
redneck,

825
00:43:18,367 --> 00:43:20,767
极端保守基督教的美国南部地区，
引来最大的仇恨和关注。”
deeply Christian
part of the Union.

826
00:43:20,867 --> 00:43:22,100
装饰？
Decorate?

827
00:43:22,133 --> 00:43:24,367
我想这意思是，我们得在
对方的车上写标语，所以你……
I think what it means is
we each have to write slogans

828
00:43:24,400 --> 00:43:26,400
-哈蒙德：好把对方害死？
-没错。
on the other one's cars,
so you...

829
00:43:26,433 --> 00:43:28,233
行啊。
-HAMMOND: To get them killed?
-Yeah.

830
00:43:28,267 --> 00:43:29,300
你来弄哈蒙德的车。
开到树丛里去弄。
All right.

831
00:43:29,333 --> 00:43:31,100
-你弄……
-我来弄你的车。
You do Hammond's.
Take it away into the bushes.

832
00:43:31,133 --> 00:43:32,267
我今天非害死你不可。
行了，麻溜点！
-You do...
-I'm doing yours.

833
00:43:32,300 --> 00:43:34,500
美国南方，南方啊……
信基督教、留寸头、
I'm getting you killed.
Well, come on!

834
00:43:39,333 --> 00:43:43,100
讨厌共产党。
The south, the south.
It is Christian, short hair,

835
00:43:43,133 --> 00:43:45,133
他们最在意的是什么呢？
they don't like Communists.

836
00:43:45,167 --> 00:43:46,867
我必须得借刀杀了他，
这可是一辈子难遇的绝佳机会。
What is closest
to their heart?

837
00:43:46,867 --> 00:43:49,267
要是不整死他，我都对不起你、
对不起我自己、对不起所有人。
I've gotta get him killed.
This is a once
in a lifetime opportunity.

838
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:51,933
（大笑）
I'd be letting you down,
me down, everybody down.

839
00:43:52,700 --> 00:43:54,400
哈蒙德：平时总拿我身高开涮，
这下遭报应了吧！
(LAUGHING)

840
00:43:55,933 --> 00:43:58,233
哈蒙德：这仇报的是那些身高梗。
HAMMOND: Revenge for
all those height gags.

841
00:43:58,267 --> 00:44:00,067
这算报答他每次
叫我“鼹鼠”的仇。
Every time
he's called me Hamster.

842
00:44:00,100 --> 00:44:03,100
这是罚你每次
迟到外加迷路。
This is for every time
you've been late and lost.

843
00:44:03,133 --> 00:44:04,967
看出来写的是啥了吗？
Can you tell what it says yet?

844
00:44:06,400 --> 00:44:07,533
（口哨声）
(WHISTLING)

845
00:44:15,267 --> 00:44:17,633
詹姆斯，我恨死你这招了，
真的恨死你了。
James, I hate you for that.
I really hate you for that.

846
00:44:17,667 --> 00:44:20,133
-谁让你老是追尾
撞我的凯迪拉克。
-就是。
-All the time you drove
into the back of my Cadillac.
-Yeah.

847
00:44:20,167 --> 00:44:24,333
说实话，凭良心讲，
我觉得大家这回
都干得挺漂亮。
Do you know, actually,
I think, honestly, we've all
done a good job here.

848
00:44:24,367 --> 00:44:28,267
但我敢打赌，
最有可能挨枪子的，
But I do believe
that the person
most likely to be shot

849
00:44:28,300 --> 00:44:29,667
绝对是哈蒙德。
is indeed Hammond.

850
00:44:29,700 --> 00:44:31,767
-原因很简单……
-詹姆斯，我觉得你刚才干的，
-The simple...
-I think what
you've done there James,

851
00:44:31,867 --> 00:44:34,067
-是亲手害死了你的朋友。
-确实。
-is killed your friend.
-Yeah.

852
00:44:34,100 --> 00:44:37,233
克拉克森：我们提心吊胆地
重新驶上了公路。
CLARKSON: Gingerly,
we rejoined the open road.

853
00:44:39,867 --> 00:44:41,900
在这一带，有三大信仰：
Three religions
down here,

854
00:44:41,933 --> 00:44:45,733
乔治·布什、上帝、
还有乡村与西部音乐。
George Bush, God,
Country and Western.

855
00:44:45,767 --> 00:44:48,533
就按这个顺序，
地位依次上升。
In that order,
ascending order.

856
00:45:03,367 --> 00:45:07,467
说老实话，我这辈子
都没这么扎眼过。
I'll be honest. I have felt
less conspicuous than this.

857
00:45:18,400 --> 00:45:21,133
到了，
“甜蜜的家乡阿拉巴马”。
Here we are.
Sweet home Alabama.

858
00:45:21,867 --> 00:45:23,533
（模仿枪声）
(IMITATES GUNFIRE)

859
00:45:30,433 --> 00:45:33,033
克拉克森：
他们连自家的路牌都开枪射！
CLARKSON:
They've shot their own sign!

860
00:45:33,067 --> 00:45:35,400
那他们会对我们干出什么来？
What are they gonna do to us?

861
00:45:55,033 --> 00:45:57,733
要想明白杰里米
究竟对我这辆车下了什么毒手，
To understand what Jeremy
has actually done to my car,

862
00:45:57,767 --> 00:46:01,600
你就得记住，
这里可是共和党的
深红大本营。
you have to remember
that this is deep
Republican territory.

863
00:46:01,633 --> 00:46:07,033
而那个女人（希拉里）
可是民主党魁首，
简直就是敌基督降世。
That woman
is the arch Democrat.
She is the anti-Christ.

864
00:46:07,067 --> 00:46:09,267
哈蒙德：
还不仅仅是标语的问题，
HAMMOND:
It's not just the slogan.

865
00:46:09,300 --> 00:46:13,400
关键它还被涂在皮卡上，
那可是美国南方的灵魂象征啊，
It's the fact that
it's painted on a pick-up,
symbol of the South,

866
00:46:13,433 --> 00:46:15,333
-我是说……
-（汽车鸣笛声）
-I mean...
-(HORN BLARES)

867
00:46:15,367 --> 00:46:16,400
哦呦！
Ooh!

868
00:46:18,300 --> 00:46:21,367
梅：接着，杰里米还在后备箱上写了：
“纳斯卡烂透了”。
MAY: And then, Jeremy
has written on the boot,
"NASCAR sucks."

869
00:46:21,400 --> 00:46:23,000
那可是一种房车赛事，
That's a type of
saloon car racing

870
00:46:23,033 --> 00:46:25,133
在这片地方简直火到没边。
that is very, very big
in this part of the world.

871
00:46:25,167 --> 00:46:27,100
所有车手都是这儿走出去的，
This is where all
the drivers come from,

872
00:46:27,133 --> 00:46:28,733
赛车全是在这儿造出来的，
all the building
of the cars is done,

873
00:46:28,767 --> 00:46:30,467
铁杆车迷也全扎堆在这一带，
all the supporters
come from down here,

874
00:46:30,500 --> 00:46:32,333
你跑来说纳斯卡烂透了，
and to say it sucks,

875
00:46:32,367 --> 00:46:35,500
无异于当面冲上去
给人家神圣的老母亲一记重拳。
is a bit like
going up and punching
somebody's sainted mother.

876
00:46:40,433 --> 00:46:42,867
别！别啊！
No! No!

877
00:46:43,633 --> 00:46:45,433
-（汽车鸣笛声）
-哇啊！
-(HORN BLARES)
-Whoa!

878
00:46:46,433 --> 00:46:47,900
（汽车鸣笛声）
(HORN BLARES)

879
00:46:52,333 --> 00:46:54,033
克拉克森：
我们好歹在高速路上捡回了一条小命，
CLARKSON:
We've survived the highway,

880
00:46:54,067 --> 00:46:57,033
但紧接着，我们不得不拐进镇子里加油。
but then we had to
pull into a town for fuel.

881
00:47:03,767 --> 00:47:07,500
噢，这可真是
太吓人了。
Oh, this is
really terrifying.

882
00:47:15,467 --> 00:47:17,533
行吧！
Okay!

883
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:21,467
只是，呃……
那是柴油。
Just, um...
That's diesel.

884
00:47:22,033 --> 00:47:23,967
那是……我加成了……
That's... I've gone...

885
00:47:25,167 --> 00:47:29,267
“选希拉里当总统”
这标语反应很不妙啊。
"Hillary for President"
that's not going down well.

886
00:47:29,300 --> 00:47:33,500
克拉克森：这位女士很生气。
但还不如
加油站的老板娘生气。
CLARKSON: This lady was cross.
But not as cross
as the garage's owner.

887
00:47:33,533 --> 00:47:35,100
我来问你！
I'll ask you!

888
00:47:35,867 --> 00:47:37,367
你们到底是不是搞基的，
Now are you all gay,

889
00:47:37,400 --> 00:47:39,333
特意来看看
在乡巴佬小镇待多久
会被人痛揍一顿？
hooking to see
how long it takes
to get beat up in a hick town?

890
00:47:40,333 --> 00:47:42,067
克拉克森：
我不是同性恋。我结了婚的。
CLARKSON:
I'm not gay. I'm married.

891
00:47:42,100 --> 00:47:43,600
我有三个孩子。
I've got three children.

892
00:47:43,633 --> 00:47:45,667
不，我们真不是。没有的事。
No, we are not. No.

893
00:47:45,700 --> 00:47:49,300
我们只是……
以一种与众不同的方式
装饰了一下车子。
We've just sort of
decorated our cars
in a distinctive manner.

894
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:53,067
“纳斯卡赛车烂透了”，
“乡村音乐
是垃圾”？
"NASCAR sucks",
"Country and Western
is rubbish?"

895
00:47:53,100 --> 00:47:55,167
你猜怎么着？
老兄，你们可是在乡巴佬小镇。
Guess what?
You're on a hick town, man.

896
00:47:55,200 --> 00:47:56,667
我们今天死定了。
全完了。
We're gonna die now.
That's it.

897
00:47:56,700 --> 00:47:59,200
你敢动一下试试！（哔——）
Don't you dare! (BLEEP)

898
00:47:59,233 --> 00:48:01,600
哈蒙德：她说
她要去叫弟兄们过来了。
HAMMOND: She said
she was gonna get the boys.

899
00:48:01,633 --> 00:48:02,700
我先撤了！
I'm gone!

900
00:48:02,867 --> 00:48:06,233
于是我们决定赶紧开溜。
So we decided to scarper.

901
00:48:06,267 --> 00:48:09,933
我才刚想起来。
其实我的油
还多得很呢。
I've just remembered.
I've actually got
loads of petrol.

902
00:48:09,967 --> 00:48:11,300
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

903
00:48:13,933 --> 00:48:16,133
哈蒙德：然后，
偏偏挑在最要命的节骨眼上。
HAMMOND: And then,
of all the moments.

904
00:48:16,167 --> 00:48:18,367
-喂，搭电线！
-你开玩笑吧？
-Oye, jump leads!
-You're joking?

905
00:48:18,400 --> 00:48:19,867
搭电线！
Jump leads.

906
00:48:19,867 --> 00:48:21,300
别挑现在啊！
Not now!

907
00:48:25,967 --> 00:48:28,867
这将是
史上最快的一次搭电救援。
This is gonna be
the quickest jump in history.

908
00:48:28,867 --> 00:48:31,133
你去拿电线。
我来打火。
You get the leads.
I'll start it.

909
00:48:31,167 --> 00:48:34,000
告诉你朋友，要是他
敢在我的停车场乱涂乱画……
Tell your friend if he
tagged up my parking lot...

910
00:48:34,033 --> 00:48:35,967
哈蒙德：红脖子们杀到了。
HAMMOND: The rednecks arrived.

911
00:48:37,333 --> 00:48:38,967
我们这儿出了点小状况。
We've just got
a slight problem here.

912
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:41,067
（嘈杂的叫喊声）
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

913
00:48:42,567 --> 00:48:44,333
大事不妙！
This is bad!

914
00:48:44,367 --> 00:48:46,367
接着他们把矛头
对准了摄制组！
Then they turned
on the film crews!

915
00:48:46,400 --> 00:48:50,100
（嘈杂的叫喊声）
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

916
00:48:50,133 --> 00:48:51,533
快点！
Quick!

917
00:48:51,567 --> 00:48:54,067
（叫喊声持续）
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

918
00:48:54,100 --> 00:48:56,500
石头开始
朝我们的工作车狂砸。
Rocks started
pelting our vans.

919
00:48:57,900 --> 00:49:00,300
男人：快滚！滚出这里！
MAN: Go! Get out of here!

920
00:49:01,033 --> 00:49:02,567
怎么回事？
What's happening?

921
00:49:08,700 --> 00:49:09,867
（哔——）
(BLEEP)

922
00:49:09,867 --> 00:49:11,400
（引擎启动声）
(ENGINE STARTING)

923
00:49:13,700 --> 00:49:14,900
在接下来的几分钟里，
For the next few moments,

924
00:49:14,933 --> 00:49:17,933
我们的电视节目
变成了电台广播。
our TV programme
became a radio show.

925
00:49:17,967 --> 00:49:22,333
哦，（哔——）
那些皮卡追上来了！
Oh, (BLEEP)
there are the pick-up trucks.

926
00:49:22,367 --> 00:49:26,367
油门踩到底！
我看屁股后头
跟了一大群。
Get your foot down.
I think we've got
a load of them on our tail.

927
00:49:28,333 --> 00:49:30,100
我跟你们说，
情况绝对不对劲。
Something's going on here,
I'm telling you.

928
00:49:30,133 --> 00:49:32,900
刚才在加油站的
那三辆皮卡，
Because these three trucks,
that were
in the petrol station

929
00:49:32,933 --> 00:49:35,533
刚刚超过去
冲到我们前头了。
have now just
torn past us.

930
00:49:35,567 --> 00:49:38,033
弟兄们，咱们必须
把这些标语擦掉！
We need to get
these slogans off, lads.

931
00:49:38,633 --> 00:49:39,933
靠边停，靠边停！
Pull over, pull over.

932
00:49:46,367 --> 00:49:47,867
擦另一边！
Get the other side.

933
00:49:49,267 --> 00:49:51,133
没东西可以擦了！
Nothing to wipe it off
with now.

934
00:49:54,433 --> 00:49:55,433
快走！
Go.

935
00:49:57,433 --> 00:50:01,500
克拉克森：
“大作”被抹掉后，
我们开始亡命狂飙。
CLARKSON:
With the artwork gone,
we hit the road, hard.

936
00:50:04,667 --> 00:50:06,733
我正在做一件
做梦都想不到会干的事。
I'm doing something
I never thought I'd do.

937
00:50:06,767 --> 00:50:08,333
老子正在往州界逃命！
I am running for the border.

938
00:50:09,467 --> 00:50:11,533
苍天啊，
刚才真的吓死人了。
God in heaven,
that was actually frightening.

939
00:50:12,933 --> 00:50:15,367
他们刚才真会宰了我们的！
They could have killed us!

940
00:50:15,400 --> 00:50:17,967
克拉克森：他们真的
毫无反讽细胞。
CLARKSON: They really do have
an irony deficiency.

941
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:20,733
我真心觉得，
在如今美国的某些犄角旮旯，
I honestly believe
that in certain parts
of America now,

942
00:50:20,767 --> 00:50:24,233
这帮人已经开始
跟蔬菜杂交了。
people have started to mate
with vegetables.

943
00:50:24,267 --> 00:50:28,233
然而刚甩掉一个大麻烦，
我们又一头撞进了另一个麻烦里。
And then
with one problem behind us,
we ran straight into another.

944
00:50:30,167 --> 00:50:31,500
天啊，闪电！
God, lightning!

945
00:50:32,733 --> 00:50:35,600
你们觉得这是上帝
在惩罚我们吗？
You think this is God
punishing us?

946
00:50:35,633 --> 00:50:37,600
-我只是……
-（雷声轰鸣）
-I'm just...
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)

947
00:50:38,767 --> 00:50:40,800
听见那声音了吗？
Did you hear that?

948
00:50:45,867 --> 00:50:47,467
真是个发现真相的
绝佳时机——
It was a great time
to discover

949
00:50:47,500 --> 00:50:50,700
我车上的雨刮器
根本连摆设都不如。
that the wipers in my car
were worse than useless.

950
00:50:50,733 --> 00:50:53,800
这简直就是
恐怖片里的桥段。
This is like something
out of a horror film now.

951
00:50:57,267 --> 00:51:02,333
我有大麻烦了。
我眼前一片漆黑，什么都看不清！
I'm in serious trouble.
I cannot see a damn thing.

952
00:51:02,367 --> 00:51:04,767
路上一座出口都没有，
如果在应急车道停车，
There were no exits and
stopping on the hard shoulder

953
00:51:04,867 --> 00:51:07,033
在这么大的暴雨天
纯属自寻死路。
in rain like this
would've been suicidal.

954
00:51:07,067 --> 00:51:10,233
所以只剩
唯一的办法了。
So there was
only one choice.

955
00:51:10,267 --> 00:51:12,133
你压线了！
往右打，杰里米！
You're on the lane.
Go right, Jeremy.

956
00:51:12,167 --> 00:51:15,867
得嘞，这下可彻底要命了！
Yeah, now, this is very bad!

957
00:51:16,767 --> 00:51:18,600
往左偏一点。
Left a bit.

958
00:51:18,633 --> 00:51:21,867
求求你别下了，
求求你停吧，
别再下了！
Please stop raining,
please stop raining,
please stop raining.

959
00:51:21,900 --> 00:51:23,900
哈蒙德：你压线了！
往右打！
HAMMOND: You're on the lane.
Go right.

960
00:51:23,933 --> 00:51:26,700
我想我干脆
跳车自我了断算了，
I think I am just gonna
get out and kill myself,

961
00:51:26,733 --> 00:51:28,333
给自己个痛快算了。
put myself out of misery.

962
00:51:28,367 --> 00:51:30,233
见鬼了。
Oh, hell.

963
00:51:41,267 --> 00:51:43,867
又是狂风暴雨，
又是砸石头的红脖子乡巴佬，
What with the storm and
the rock-throwing rednecks,

964
00:51:43,900 --> 00:51:47,133
我们这趟“飞机+自驾”度假游
实在算不上顺利。
our fly-drive holiday
wasn't going that well.

965
00:51:47,167 --> 00:51:51,133
我现在只想爬上
英国航空的大喷气机
麻溜儿回家。
I just wanted to get
on the big British jet
and go home.

966
00:51:54,100 --> 00:51:58,533
我真想一上机就被一位
穿灰色法兰绒长裤的男同空少迎接，
听他对我说：
I want to be met
by a homosexual in grey
flannel trousers saying,

967
00:51:58,567 --> 00:52:01,400
“欢迎登机，克拉克森先生。
需要给您来块司康饼吗？”
"Welcome on board,
Mr. Clarkson.
Can I get you a scone?"

968
00:52:06,633 --> 00:52:09,300
离新奥尔良还有111英里。
111 miles to New Orleans.

969
00:52:09,333 --> 00:52:10,400
撑住啊，科迈罗！
Come on, Camaro!

970
00:52:13,533 --> 00:52:14,933
哈蒙德：太棒了，到了！
HAMMOND: Yes, that's it!

971
00:52:14,967 --> 00:52:16,367
我们进路易斯安那州了。
We're in Louisiana.

972
00:52:20,200 --> 00:52:23,867
詹姆斯：接下来只要开到那儿，
把车卖掉就行了。
MAY: All we had to do was
get there and sell our cars.

973
00:52:38,233 --> 00:52:42,533
而那一刻，说实在的，
会挺让人伤感的。
And that, actually,
would be quite a sad moment.

974
00:52:42,567 --> 00:52:46,533
我爱我的凯迪拉克。
I love my Cadillac.

975
00:52:46,567 --> 00:52:49,433
我是说，我们俩相识才……
多长时间，几天而已，
I mean, we've known
each other, what, a few days

976
00:52:49,467 --> 00:52:51,767
却一起经历了这趟
精彩绝伦的冒险，
we had this fantastic
adventure together

977
00:52:51,867 --> 00:52:53,033
横跨了整个美国。
all across America.

978
00:52:53,067 --> 00:52:56,033
它现在是我的车了，
虽然小毛病总是少不了。
And it's my car now,
and there are always foibles.

979
00:52:56,067 --> 00:52:57,333
哈蒙德：它不是块头最大的皮卡，
HAMMOND: It's not
the biggest truck,

980
00:52:57,367 --> 00:52:59,667
不是跑得最快的，也不是最好看的，
it's not the fastest,
it's not the best looking,

981
00:52:59,700 --> 00:53:01,433
但它就是能一直死撑着往前跑。
but it just keeps going.

982
00:53:01,467 --> 00:53:03,167
简直就像一匹威尔士小矮马。
It's like a little Welsh pony.

983
00:53:04,233 --> 00:53:05,667
这一点我很佩服。
I respect that.

984
00:53:05,700 --> 00:53:09,067
克拉克森：开这车真的就像
住在一栋老宅子里。
CLARKSON: This car really is
like living in an old house.

985
00:53:09,100 --> 00:53:12,367
你得摸准角度给后门来上那么一脚，
门才会开。
You know to kick the back door
in a certain way
to make it open.

986
00:53:12,400 --> 00:53:16,067
这车也是一个德行。
我知道怎么不让助力转向彻底罢工，
It's the same with this.
I know how to keep
the power steering going.

987
00:53:16,100 --> 00:53:19,233
也知道怎么把残存离合器的
最后一丝力气榨出来。
I know how to get the best out
of what's left of the clutch.

988
00:53:19,267 --> 00:53:21,167
刚出发时我只是把它当成个笑话，
I liked it as a kind of joke
when we started

989
00:53:21,200 --> 00:53:25,367
